{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"ca6836fc199edb54","type":"text","text":"## 5. Environmental encounters\n\nKeep\n\n![Ecco la nostra demo commentata di Little Nightmares 2](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/A-CtF2HG4nmfQ1RmFbAkAhq3o3XiH18wrRX32Ttbtx4KgVmwdIwaVDGIUI79DhKJFXnCGeEvDFO3wBRl4CCDW3jfkXmlRikwvjJpiZmjyFuA5-EHySZPKa4k_zHga6HQBYiAixj4iCo1KevU2b2ExcMM9bjrywdqOYgMj0j0mvs?purpose=inline)\n\nInspired by: Little Nightmares\n\nEncounters where the player must make a decision, escape or interact with something dangerous.\n\nImplementation:\n\n- 5-8 handcrafted encounters.\n    \n- Each encounter has 2-3 possible choices.\n    \n- Choices can affect sanity, NPC relationships or inventory.\n    \n- Some encounters are only available at certain sanity levels.\n    \n\nNo complicated combat system. No advanced enemy AI. Just scripted encounters.","x":-1700,"y":-580,"width":740,"height":920},
		{"id":"6ecf2be2d31b3dd2","x":-1693,"y":-1620,"width":813,"height":843,"type":"text","text":"## 2. Small interconnected world\n\nKeep\n\n![Design Folio](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/IdeqNGazJu82RWpwXUjTuv-uEdtuPBKMubRDvSUy7Ez42S1Q31ybf7tZFqoDii1u5dcw6XcSw0WccIsLD87eDb-kRm_twqJ5ueVIBcrkilW0Xlpk_hhLN-QZxASs4V9tqU57bj3e7effmBWiXh6k7x2e04QaEXQ4JyXoZG2gkaw?purpose=inline)\n\nInspired by: Hollow Knight\n\nBuild a small world with interconnected areas, shortcuts and locked paths.\n\nImplementation:\n\n- One central forest.\n    \n- 3 distinct areas branching off from it.\n    \n- Each area has one requirement to access.\n    \n- Shortcuts unlock as you explore.\n    \n\nDon't procedurally generate anything. Handcrafted areas are much easier to manage."},
		{"id":"1331838bf26ea291","x":-742,"y":-560,"width":682,"height":800,"type":"text","text":"## 3. Temporary safe spaces\n\nKeep\n\n![Steam Community :: Guide :: How To Create A Impenetrable Fortress of Furniture in Darkwood](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/kS1LOBxVZD2ovLXB25rYX_3IEiIML0bTnxgK3cNjb4nm-tzm5Po0A14bYqbfRZz889gRZ5nMXg8NZvQY7qaY88igF-4XqjINmdgpQqOWMZxgKDFWCdjcx2zZNNPex6Czx8Z8FBxmzMBNhwl5o6OdYC-c0yROwaUmwnPehJ0Fvyk?purpose=inline)\n\nInspired by: Darkwood\n\nSafe spaces restore sanity and provide somewhere to interact with NPCs.\n\nImplementation:\n\n- Entering a sanctuary restores 15 sanity the first time.\n    \n- Interacting with certain objects restores additional sanity.\n    \n- Each sanctuary has one NPC or interesting interaction.\n    \n- Sanctuaries are fixed locations, not dynamically generated.\n    \n\nI'd avoid having safe spaces randomly become unsafe. That's additional AI and event logic you don't need initially.\n"},
		{"id":"6d0dab775357f87d","x":-720,"y":-1600,"width":755,"height":794,"type":"text","text":"## 1. Sanity changes dialogue and perception\n\nKeep\n\n![Disco Elysium: Talk to Joyce about the Pale without Kim - walkthrough - gamepressure.com](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/t2M8Vk9chpgYPAwldwa8Ei8tXboVnHJyj7qzk9_EyFyC6RttzEihQHCsZK9rcO_FCUAgrgFS4gPtUFQ__y0HOwb0sS6EzZOMpkk9GWM2YuImASMXRQXYFuQnKyKZS4m5ZFtJBrvkUkGBMlXLe6t3hOScStbeg2WhXdZiXRXLidI?purpose=inline)\n\nInspired by: Disco Elysium\n\nOne sanity variable determines which dialogue options are available and occasionally changes how NPCs appear.\n\nImplementation:\n\n- One sanity value between 0 and 100.\n    \n- Certain events increase or decrease it.\n    \n- Dialogue options have minimum sanity requirements.\n    \n- At low sanity, some dialogue options are replaced with alternative ones.\n    \n\nExample:\n\nAn NPC asks you where you came from.\n\n- High sanity: \"I don't remember.\"\n    \n- Low sanity: \"You know where. You sent me here.\"\n    \n\nYou don't need elaborate hallucination AI or complicated systems. Just different dialogue conditions."},
		{"id":"b09bcb395e27ca89","x":240,"y":-1600,"width":1109,"height":1041,"type":"text","text":"## 4. Favors and NPC relationships\n\nKeep\n\n![Bombers’ Notebook: Link the Goron (Majora’s Mask) - Zelda Universe](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/2XYGEmdZoKZKQ5EUI_dOohjf0LK9fdsyVmVqJJGfAW8BPjIRrTBDx2pxg4ZnLtnCcjAiJhNRqAInhV9xMMoUPWCPqDCFom1uq4bKaSSeoWe24iz7da6mqyagi9BHF_hnNr48Z1bWPHCEU1KYwHTf3OCt9A1bKVXu-3XAxzc3ss4?purpose=inline)\n\nInspired by: Majora's Mask\n\nNPCs offer small tasks, and your decisions influence their opinion of you.\n\nImplementation:\n\n- 4-5 important NPCs.\n    \n- Each NPC has a simple relationship value.\n    \n- Each NPC offers 1-2 favors.\n    \n- Completing favors rewards you with items, information or access to locations.\n    \n- NPC dialogue changes depending on your relationship.\n    \n\nNo elaborate reputation simulation. Just a few variables and conditional dialogue."},
		{"id":"558295fcb1fec8ff","x":-1440,"y":-1800,"width":480,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"# VERY COOL AI STUFF"}
	],
	"edges":[]
}